cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Awesome Agentic Use Cases: verified agentic AI use cases with
  evals, measured cost, and observed failure modes
message: >-
  If you use this repository, its evaluation harness, or the
  failure taxonomy in your work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Imran
    family-names: Ahamed
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # add if you have one
repository-code: 'https://github.com/immu4989/awesome-agentic-usecases'
url: 'https://github.com/immu4989/awesome-agentic-usecases'
abstract: >-
  A collection of agentic AI use cases in which every entry ships
  with the harness that verifies it: an evaluation set with
  programmatic ground truth generated from a seed, cost per run
  computed from measured token usage, results across repeated runs
  with paired bootstrap confidence intervals, and failure modes
  that were observed in committed runs rather than hypothesised.
  Worlds are synthetic by design, which buys exact ground truth
  and lets any result be reproduced at zero cost on free model
  tiers, and which limits external validity accordingly. The
  repository also contains a cross-cutting taxonomy of agent
  failure patterns derived from the observed failures.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - agent-evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - failure-analysis
  - prompt-injection
  - tool-use
license: Apache-2.0
